sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: A session turn uses separate command and event channels
  accDescr: The client subscribes to a resumable stream, posts a message, and receives a 202 receipt. A dispatcher queues or starts the turn. Runtime events reach every subscriber independently of the POST response.
  participant C as DorkOS client
  participant H as HTTP + stream routes
  participant D as MessageDispatcher
  participant R as AgentRuntime
  C->>H: Open /api/sessions/:id/events (WebSocket)
  H->>R: Snapshot + subscribe
  R-->>H: Snapshot + live event subscription
  H-->>C: Snapshot, then live events
  C->>H: POST /api/sessions/:id/messages
  H->>D: Dispatch message
  D->>D: Persist queue when needed
  D-->>H: Acceptance receipt
  H-->>C: 202 + canonical sessionId + receipt
  Note over C,D: 202 means accepted. turn_start means running.<br/>Receipt and live events can race.
  D->>R: Start when session can accept a turn
  R-->>H: turn_start → deltas / tools → turn_end
  H-->>C: Forward ordered events
  Note over H,C: Route fans events out to all subscribed clients
  C->>H: Reconnect with opaque resume cursor
  H-->>C: Replay gap, or fresh snapshot if cursor is stale
  Note over C,H: App: WebSocket ?resume= · HTTP consumers: SSE Last-Event-ID
